title Fold AD -- the quarrel cluster, and the fold that cost one word
prompt Autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, one council-rota doc deep-read, send the increment as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. The REDS ledger stands at 110 rows and its newest, REDS %110, reads CLOSED at 20260821.073606 -- the carry-meter prose rule made a property rather than a phrase. No open agent-closable red stands, so the constructive queue is free.
think Council rota, lap index 592 kyri logs mod 27 -> item 25, active-designing/20260816-205859_double-seat-expansion-eight-seasons.md. Deep-read. It confirms the seat this arc runs under and names the floor it builds on: the crypto surface and the open image module are landed and green, and the eight seasons rest on a ladder that must stay readable. A ladder carrying a hundred thousand duplicated lines is the opposite of that floor, so the fold arc is Lindy work rather than tidying.
think The running thread came off the newest log's recommend line: the printed queue named refer_the_quarrel at 21 rungs by 72 lines, 1,440 carried, with escort_the_word behind it -- and the standing instruction to hash the family before trusting the count, then read the reach closure for whole families rather than merely for words to widen.
think Hashed every refer_the_quarrel on the ladder. Twenty-two bodies at seventy-two lines: twenty-one byte for byte alike, and refer.rye apart by nine lines, every one of the nine the same shape -- the owner reaches its own report directly where every rung above reaches through refer_of. Third tier owner in four laps to wear that signature, after amend.rye and appeal.rye. It stays home.
think Fold Z's rule ran before scope was chosen, and reported the plainest number this arc has seen: refer_the_quarrel reaches eighteen symbols and all eighteen already stood public in all twenty-one rungs. The main fold cost no widening at all.
think Reading one hop out found six of those eighteen standing as whole carrying families -- position_standing in twenty-seven, dwell_published in twenty-four, and forum_published, refer_refusal, case_delivered, refer_note in twenty-two each. All six lifted. The whole seven-family lap cost exactly one widened word, case_path, shared by case_delivered and refer_note.
obs The first fold script attempt kept the signature line deliberately after the last lap booked a pass that had dropped it. One delegate was read by hand before the other one hundred fifty-two were trusted.
obs The arithmetic closes with no remainder. Out went 20x72, 26x12, 23x16, 21x13, 21x12, 21x13, 21x10 at 3,128; back came the same seven cohorts at three lines apiece, 459; the fall of 2,669 stood against a meter reading 2,669. Fold AC's extra twenty-six came from a family that widening split in two -- this lap widened a word inside a family already whole, so nothing split and nothing was gained by accident.
obs Six further reached bodies stayed home, and the README says so honestly rather than by rule. endures, stands_loud, unheard_outside, referred_in, unreferred_in, is_party, refer_holds, referral_bytes, and settlement_published each run three to seven lines where a delegate runs three. They still carry a few hundred lines between them, so the honest claim is that the gain is small rather than that it is zero.
obs Three elder README lines normalized British to American spelling under the on-touch ratchet, one of them a heading. Grepped the tree for inbound anchor references first and found none, so no promise broke.
obs The lesson this lap adds is that a free fold is a signal rather than luck. The appeal, dependent, reap, and amendment clusters had each widened the symbols this tier shares, so by the time the quarrel came up the queue its whole neighborhood was already open. Folds pay forward, and the queue ordered by carried lines alone walks a tier in roughly that order because a tier's families rise together.
